1
00:00:49,321 --> 00:00:52,071
He put up a valiant fight

2
00:00:52,151 --> 00:00:54,531
against a group of English soldiers.

3
00:00:55,571 --> 00:00:58,321
But he was stabbed from behind with a spear,
and tragically...

4
00:00:59,161 --> 00:01:02,161
Please accept my sincere condolences,
Your Highness.

5
00:01:06,371 --> 00:01:09,501
We were eating rabbit stew,

6
00:01:09,591 --> 00:01:11,551
and then he left suddenly.

7
00:01:16,841 --> 00:01:18,141
That's weird.

8
00:01:18,221 --> 00:01:19,471
Just now...

9
00:01:20,511 --> 00:01:21,601
But...

10
00:01:26,021 --> 00:01:27,771
We shall leave immediately.

11
00:01:27,851 --> 00:01:28,851
Get ready.

12
00:01:29,521 --> 00:01:30,441
Thorfinn.

13
00:01:30,521 --> 00:01:32,401
Don't leave him alone.

14
00:01:32,481 --> 00:01:36,741
What? You're kidding me! I don't want to!

15
00:01:36,821 --> 00:01:38,111
Hey! Wait!

16
00:01:38,201 --> 00:01:40,991
Guarding the prince is your job!

17
00:01:41,081 --> 00:01:42,281
No!

18
00:03:17,591 --> 00:03:19,761
He's paralyzed with fear.

19
00:03:19,841 --> 00:03:22,471
Is that weakling of a prince going to be okay?

20
00:03:22,931 --> 00:03:25,261
I think your plan backfired, Askeladd.

21
00:03:25,351 --> 00:03:27,011
Maybe you shouldn't have killed Ragnar.

22
00:03:27,101 --> 00:03:28,431
HISTORY OF BEASTS

23
00:03:28,521 --> 00:03:30,141
Don't talk so loudly.

24
00:03:30,771 --> 00:03:33,441
Most of the men don't know what really happened.

25
00:03:33,521 --> 00:03:36,441
The English are the ones who did it.

26
00:03:36,521 --> 00:03:37,651
Don't let the secret out.

27
00:03:37,731 --> 00:03:39,901
I wonder...

28
00:03:39,991 --> 00:03:43,031
Everyone knows you didn't get along with Ragnar.

29
00:03:43,111 --> 00:03:45,531
He may be weak, but he's going to realize
what happened.

30
00:03:45,621 --> 00:03:48,411
As long as there's no proof, it will be fine.

31
00:03:48,491 --> 00:03:50,121
The reason the prince is so weak

32
00:03:50,201 --> 00:03:52,411
is because Ragnar spoiled him.

33
00:03:52,501 --> 00:03:54,581
I had to make Ragnar disappear.

34
00:03:54,671 --> 00:03:56,291
Otherwise, he'd cause me grief.

35
00:03:56,381 --> 00:03:58,551
The fact that he's weak is a good thing.

36
00:03:58,631 --> 00:04:00,171
It makes him easy to control.

37
00:04:00,261 --> 00:04:03,551
He can be used as the perfect stepping stone
to achieve greatness in the world.

38
00:04:07,851 --> 00:04:08,721
Bjorn.

39
00:04:09,891 --> 00:04:12,851
Why have you served me for all this time?

40
00:04:14,271 --> 00:04:16,901
Well, it's...

41
00:04:16,981 --> 00:04:18,981
because I wanted to.

42
00:04:19,691 --> 00:04:20,861
I'm the same.

43
00:04:21,861 --> 00:04:24,321
I choose my own lord too.

44
00:04:24,411 --> 00:04:25,611
My lord

45
00:04:25,701 --> 00:04:28,871
must be the type of man that makes me want
to serve him.

46
00:04:31,291 --> 00:04:32,621
Just kidding.

47
00:04:34,501 --> 00:04:36,671
I'm making a gamble, Bjorn.

48
00:04:36,751 --> 00:04:38,211
If we get lucky,

49
00:04:38,291 --> 00:04:41,421
that prince might completely change.

50
00:04:41,511 --> 00:04:43,591
What are you going to do if you don't get lucky?

51
00:04:44,171 --> 00:04:48,351
He might
get depressed and never recover.

52
00:04:48,971 --> 00:04:51,061
If that happens, I'll abandon him.

53
00:04:51,641 --> 00:04:53,931
He wouldn't deserve to be my lord.

54
00:05:02,691 --> 00:05:04,951
How's it going? Is he going to crack?

55
00:05:05,321 --> 00:05:07,491
He pisses me off.

56
00:05:07,571 --> 00:05:09,451
He won't even scream.

57
00:05:09,911 --> 00:05:12,041
He thinks he's a martyr.

58
00:05:12,121 --> 00:05:15,161
This is why I hate Christians.

59
00:05:15,541 --> 00:05:18,081
You didn't kick him hard enough.

60
00:05:18,171 --> 00:05:19,751
I'll show you how to do it.

61
00:05:20,791 --> 00:05:22,631
This is how you kick!

62
00:05:24,881 --> 00:05:26,051
Like this!

63
00:05:27,051 --> 00:05:28,261
Good job.

64
00:05:28,341 --> 00:05:29,801
You're bad at kicking too.

65
00:05:29,891 --> 00:05:31,061
Kick him in the jaw.

66
00:05:31,141 --> 00:05:33,101
Wait! It's my turn next!

67
00:05:33,181 --> 00:05:34,141
Stop!

68
00:05:34,271 --> 00:05:35,601
Come on!

69
00:05:35,681 --> 00:05:38,191
Don't overdo it, you guys!

70
00:05:38,601 --> 00:05:41,151
If you kill him, we can't get him to talk!

71
00:05:42,151 --> 00:05:45,031
Go ahead and kill me.

72
00:05:45,741 --> 00:05:48,281
The Lord sees everything.

73
00:05:48,361 --> 00:05:52,081
He's seen all the evil things you Danes have done.

74
00:05:53,411 --> 00:05:54,951
He still has some fight left in him.

75
00:05:56,751 --> 00:05:58,121
Do you have any shears?

76
00:05:58,211 --> 00:05:59,631
Go find them.

77
00:05:59,711 --> 00:06:01,291
What?

78
00:06:01,381 --> 00:06:02,711
Shears, right?

79
00:06:05,551 --> 00:06:07,171
Well, then.

80
00:06:07,261 --> 00:06:09,641
I'll say it again, English captain.

81
00:06:11,471 --> 00:06:13,471
There are three things I want to know.

82
00:06:13,561 --> 00:06:15,431
How many reinforcements do they have?

83
00:06:15,521 --> 00:06:18,441
And how long until they get here?

84
00:06:19,351 --> 00:06:22,941
Lastly, how did they find out we're here?

85
00:06:23,481 --> 00:06:25,481
If you tell me, I'll let you live.

86
00:06:26,491 --> 00:06:29,241
You beasts!

87
00:06:30,701 --> 00:06:31,871
You bastards.

88
00:06:31,951 --> 00:06:33,831
You shall be punished.

89
00:06:33,991 --> 00:06:36,451
A death befitting of you bastards

90
00:06:36,541 --> 00:06:38,411
awaits you...

91
00:06:41,331 --> 00:06:44,961
Hey. Will these shears work?

92
00:06:45,921 --> 00:06:46,761
Yeah.

93
00:06:50,091 --> 00:06:51,511
Captain.

94
00:06:52,221 --> 00:06:55,351
Your fingernails are long.

95
00:06:56,061 --> 00:06:57,521
Long fingernails are dirty.

96
00:06:57,601 --> 00:06:59,311
You should cut them.

97
00:07:04,061 --> 00:07:05,691
Oh, sorry!

98
00:07:05,771 --> 00:07:07,151
I cut too deep.

99
00:07:08,401 --> 00:07:09,401
Hold him down.

100
00:07:10,951 --> 00:07:12,741
There are three things I want to know.

101
00:07:12,821 --> 00:07:14,451
I'll skip the rest.

102
00:07:18,121 --> 00:07:20,621
Oh, I cut too deep again!

103
00:07:20,711 --> 00:07:22,711
I did it twice!

104
00:07:23,881 --> 00:07:26,131
That's so nasty.

105
00:07:26,211 --> 00:07:28,381
What's he holding out for?

106
00:07:28,761 --> 00:07:32,301
Go to hell, you Danes!

107
00:07:32,381 --> 00:07:33,431
You bastards!

108
00:07:33,551 --> 00:07:36,641
If you bastards hadn't come...

109
00:07:37,011 --> 00:07:39,771
You bastards burned down my village!

110
00:07:39,851 --> 00:07:43,811
You tortured my wife and daughter and killed them!

111
00:07:43,901 --> 00:07:45,191
You beasts!

112
00:07:45,271 --> 00:07:49,151
This is our land! Leave!

113
00:07:50,861 --> 00:07:52,201
I see.

114
00:07:52,281 --> 00:07:54,411
We're beasts?

115
00:07:56,451 --> 00:07:57,781
You guys are ignorant.

116
00:07:57,871 --> 00:08:00,121
Let me teach you some history.

117
00:08:00,661 --> 00:08:02,371
You should thank me for sharing this,

118
00:08:02,461 --> 00:08:03,461
you Saxon.

119
00:08:04,291 --> 00:08:07,881
Or is it the Anglos who live in this area?

120
00:08:07,961 --> 00:08:10,421
Well, they're the same thing.

121
00:08:10,511 --> 00:08:12,261
This land

122
00:08:12,341 --> 00:08:14,591
didn't belong to you originally.

123
00:08:16,141 --> 00:08:18,641
The first inhabitants were the Celts.

124
00:08:18,721 --> 00:08:21,811
They lived in the forests and worshiped the spirits.

125
00:08:21,891 --> 00:08:24,481
They were the ancestors of the people
who live in Wales now.

126
00:08:25,771 --> 00:08:28,901
Then one day, the Romans came.

127
00:08:28,981 --> 00:08:30,941
They were the rulers,

128
00:08:31,031 --> 00:08:33,241
but they lived on this land alongside the Celts

129
00:08:33,321 --> 00:08:36,281
and gave them their knowledge, technology and culture.

130
00:08:37,741 --> 00:08:39,201
The Romans left,

131
00:08:39,281 --> 00:08:43,211
and then you Anglos and Saxons arrived.

132
00:08:43,291 --> 00:08:45,291
It happened 500 years ago.

133
00:08:46,331 --> 00:08:50,461
You didn't give anything to the Celts.

134
00:08:50,711 --> 00:08:51,801
Instead,

135
00:08:52,131 --> 00:08:54,551
you drove out the Celts from these fertile plains

136
00:08:54,631 --> 00:08:57,301
and forced them to live in the wastelands.

137
00:08:57,391 --> 00:08:58,431
You're lying!

138
00:08:58,641 --> 00:09:00,601
I'm not lying.

139
00:09:00,811 --> 00:09:02,851
If the Danes are beasts,

140
00:09:02,931 --> 00:09:06,691
then you Anglo-Saxons are beasts too.

141
00:09:07,731 --> 00:09:10,611
You stole these lands using violence.

142
00:09:10,691 --> 00:09:14,951
We Danes are going to steal these lands
from you using even greater violence.

143
00:09:15,951 --> 00:09:17,911
You have no objections to that, right?

144
00:09:19,281 --> 00:09:20,621
Shut up!

145
00:09:20,701 --> 00:09:24,581
I don't believe you, you savages!

146
00:09:26,711 --> 00:09:30,171
Teachers hate kids that don't listen.

147
00:09:32,341 --> 00:09:33,511
What?

148
00:09:33,591 --> 00:09:35,091
Captain.

149
00:09:35,551 --> 00:09:39,341
Now that I've got a good look at your face...

150
00:09:40,221 --> 00:09:42,261
Your nose is long.

151
00:09:45,481 --> 00:09:46,811
Askeladd!

152
00:09:53,321 --> 00:09:54,781
How many are there, Ear?

153
00:09:54,861 --> 00:09:56,991
I'm not sure. But there's a lot.

154
00:09:57,071 --> 00:09:58,611
They're coming from the south!

155
00:09:58,861 --> 00:10:00,121
Enemy reinforcements?

156
00:10:00,201 --> 00:10:01,911
In the middle of the night?

157
00:10:03,331 --> 00:10:06,461
The English are attacking at night? Impressive.

158
00:10:08,961 --> 00:10:10,041
They're here!

159
00:10:11,341 --> 00:10:14,421
It's too late! You bastards are going to die!

160
00:10:14,841 --> 00:10:18,301
I can't wait to see you Danes eat each other alive!

161
00:10:18,381 --> 00:10:20,641
-Danes?
-I'll tell you what's happening.

162
00:10:20,721 --> 00:10:22,801
Thorkell's coming!

163
00:10:22,891 --> 00:10:24,721
Not a bad match, right?

164
00:10:25,101 --> 00:10:26,351
It's Thorkell!

165
00:10:26,431 --> 00:10:29,141
Did he say Thorkell? What are we going to do?

166
00:10:29,311 --> 00:10:30,981
Hey.

167
00:10:31,061 --> 00:10:32,561
Did he say Thorkell?

168
00:10:32,651 --> 00:10:35,321
Who knows? I thought that's what he said.

169
00:10:35,571 --> 00:10:37,821
If it's true, we're in trouble.

170
00:10:38,901 --> 00:10:40,821
Thorkell?

171
00:10:40,911 --> 00:10:42,321
Did you say Thorkell?

172
00:10:42,411 --> 00:10:43,331
No way!

173
00:10:43,411 --> 00:10:44,871
Really?

174
00:10:46,501 --> 00:10:48,541
Thorkell's coming!

175
00:10:55,131 --> 00:10:56,631
Is that the village?

176
00:10:56,711 --> 00:10:58,511
That's what it looks like.

177
00:10:58,971 --> 00:11:01,471
All right! We're going to surround them!

178
00:11:01,551 --> 00:11:04,051
Vali and Ingolf's units, take the left!

179
00:11:04,141 --> 00:11:05,681
Oddr, take the right!

180
00:11:05,761 --> 00:11:07,601
I'm going to take the middle.

181
00:11:08,061 --> 00:11:10,021
Kill anyone you see!

182
00:11:10,101 --> 00:11:12,061
But don't kill the prince.

183
00:11:12,151 --> 00:11:15,021
And there should be a kid with a knife.

184
00:11:16,691 --> 00:11:18,491
Don't kill him either.

185
00:11:21,571 --> 00:11:23,911
He's my playmate.

186
00:11:24,701 --> 00:11:26,451
Thorkell's coming!

187
00:11:26,541 --> 00:11:29,041
Let me go, you buffoon!

188
00:11:29,121 --> 00:11:31,001
Are you going to disobey my orders?

189
00:11:32,081 --> 00:11:34,501
I can't leave Ragnar behind!

190
00:11:34,581 --> 00:11:37,961
I'm not going without Ragnar!

191
00:11:38,591 --> 00:11:40,551
Forget about it, Your Highness.

192
00:11:40,841 --> 00:11:44,851
We only have three sleds.
We don't have room for a corpse.

193
00:11:44,931 --> 00:11:46,931
Then let's hold a funeral for him.

194
00:11:47,011 --> 00:11:49,851
Pay your respects to the death of a warrior!
This is an order!

195
00:11:49,931 --> 00:11:52,691
We don't have enough time for that either.

196
00:11:53,731 --> 00:11:54,981
You bastard!

197
00:11:58,021 --> 00:12:01,491
No! I'm not going!

198
00:12:01,571 --> 00:12:03,991
Ragnar! Ragnar--

199
00:12:14,791 --> 00:12:19,251
Ragnar is dead. He won't come even if you call for him.

200
00:12:24,761 --> 00:12:27,051
You bastard...

201
00:12:29,471 --> 00:12:30,471
Askeladd!

202
00:12:31,141 --> 00:12:34,231
They're deserters. They were planning to join Thorkell.

203
00:12:36,611 --> 00:12:38,651
They were hiding in the straw.

204
00:12:44,781 --> 00:12:47,451
Ragnar was right!

205
00:12:47,531 --> 00:12:49,871
Luck's not on your side right now.

206
00:12:50,911 --> 00:12:52,751
We're not the only ones.

207
00:12:52,831 --> 00:12:55,961
Everyone knows we're in trouble.

208
00:12:56,041 --> 00:12:59,881
We're in big trouble this time. You're...

209
00:13:00,881 --> 00:13:03,011
Thorkell has you by the tail.

210
00:13:10,681 --> 00:13:12,351
Go ahead.

211
00:13:12,851 --> 00:13:16,651
Listen, men. Follow whichever leader you want.

212
00:13:17,521 --> 00:13:20,821
If you're going to leave, then leave!
I won't blame you.

213
00:13:20,901 --> 00:13:22,941
If you're going to come with me,

214
00:13:23,901 --> 00:13:25,151
then march!

215
00:13:27,741 --> 00:13:30,661
We're going to march until we lose Thorkell!

216
00:13:32,081 --> 00:13:35,331
Walk while you eat, and walk while you sleep!

217
00:13:36,251 --> 00:13:37,711
Listen, men!

218
00:13:37,791 --> 00:13:40,131
If you can't keep up, then you're dead.

219
00:14:12,281 --> 00:14:13,491
Wait, Thorkell!

220
00:14:13,581 --> 00:14:16,501
We're not like Askeladd.

221
00:14:16,581 --> 00:14:19,001
We want to join you--

222
00:14:27,971 --> 00:14:30,721
So, your leader's name is Askeladd?

223
00:14:34,681 --> 00:14:36,891
Oh, what a nice sword.

224
00:14:36,981 --> 00:14:40,311
-It's mine now!
-Oh, nice.

225
00:14:40,401 --> 00:14:43,361
The fact that some of their men deserted

226
00:14:43,441 --> 00:14:46,991
means they must be really worried.

227
00:14:47,071 --> 00:14:48,901
Poor things.

228
00:14:48,991 --> 00:14:51,361
You should've just let them join us.

229
00:14:51,451 --> 00:14:54,331
It's okay. They're worthless.

230
00:14:54,411 --> 00:14:58,661
I don't need cowards who surrender
without putting up a fight.

231
00:15:01,831 --> 00:15:05,671
Men, to the east! We're going to chase down the prince!

232
00:15:05,751 --> 00:15:07,841
Give it everything you got!

233
00:15:07,921 --> 00:15:09,721
Yeah!

234
00:15:15,181 --> 00:15:17,431
The right! You're too far to the right!

235
00:15:17,521 --> 00:15:19,101
Move it back.

236
00:15:19,181 --> 00:15:21,691
No! I meant my right.

237
00:15:22,811 --> 00:15:25,021
JANUARY 1014 AD
UPPER SEVERN RIVER, EARLDOM OF MERCIA

238
00:15:25,111 --> 00:15:27,651
-That's right. Keep going. Go slow.
-Heave ho!

239
00:15:27,731 --> 00:15:28,821
Hurry up!

240
00:15:28,901 --> 00:15:30,571
You're holding us up back here!

241
00:15:34,741 --> 00:15:37,541
Torgrim. Atli. Come with me.

242
00:15:37,621 --> 00:15:38,751
-Okay.
-Okay.

243
00:15:39,871 --> 00:15:42,961
Destroy this bridge. You guys take the lead.

244
00:15:43,041 --> 00:15:44,921
-Hurry.
-Okay.

245
00:15:45,341 --> 00:15:47,381
We're going to take the bridge apart.

246
00:15:47,461 --> 00:15:49,591
Pitch in if you have an ax!

247
00:15:50,381 --> 00:15:52,091
I'm so tired.

248
00:15:52,181 --> 00:15:54,471
Is Thorkell nearby, Ear?

249
00:15:54,551 --> 00:15:56,471
They're being too loud. I'm not sure.

250
00:15:56,551 --> 00:15:59,061
We might have enough time to destroy the bridge.

251
00:16:10,991 --> 00:16:13,491
Hey! Hold on! You, there, priest!

252
00:16:13,571 --> 00:16:16,031
What are you doing?

253
00:16:16,121 --> 00:16:18,161
Do you have any booze?

254
00:16:18,241 --> 00:16:21,001
Even if I did, I wouldn't give you any.

255
00:16:21,081 --> 00:16:23,421
We don't even have enough for ourselves.

256
00:16:23,501 --> 00:16:25,421
I don't have any booze for you.

257
00:16:25,501 --> 00:16:29,001
Can't you tell we're in a tight spot right now, priest?

258
00:16:45,981 --> 00:16:48,441
The water's really cold.

259
00:16:48,521 --> 00:16:51,481
Hey! This river's pretty shallow.

260
00:16:52,491 --> 00:16:54,611
They'll be able to cross it on foot!

261
00:16:54,701 --> 00:16:56,531
What's the point of destroying the bridge?

262
00:16:57,991 --> 00:17:01,161
But we can't just leave it here.

263
00:17:01,241 --> 00:17:03,461
Maybe it'll piss them off at least.

264
00:17:05,921 --> 00:17:10,751
Looks like Askeladd ran out
of those bright ideas of his.

265
00:17:19,511 --> 00:17:21,141
Bjorn! Thorfinn!

266
00:17:29,401 --> 00:17:31,191
-What's wrong?
-Come over here.

267
00:17:32,281 --> 00:17:33,191
What's going on?

268
00:17:35,201 --> 00:17:38,661
Bjorn. Move the prince over to this carriage here.

269
00:17:38,741 --> 00:17:40,491
You be the driver.

270
00:17:40,581 --> 00:17:44,081
Thorfinn, you ride with the prince. Be on standby.

271
00:17:44,161 --> 00:17:45,661
What?

272
00:17:48,171 --> 00:17:49,081
Hey!

273
00:17:50,171 --> 00:17:51,001
Askeladd!

274
00:17:52,001 --> 00:17:52,841
Are you serious?

275
00:17:55,341 --> 00:17:56,841
It's my special talent.

276
00:17:58,051 --> 00:18:00,091
I can tell what a man is like

277
00:18:00,181 --> 00:18:02,601
just by looking at his face.

278
00:18:03,221 --> 00:18:06,141
Whether he's an important man, or a nobody.
Smart, or dumb.

279
00:18:06,851 --> 00:18:11,521
I can tell that
there are some traitors among the loyal.

280
00:18:13,191 --> 00:18:14,611
What?

281
00:18:15,111 --> 00:18:16,651
Take the prince? Are you crazy?

282
00:18:16,741 --> 00:18:18,611
Idiot! Don't say it so loudly!

283
00:18:19,241 --> 00:18:20,411
Atli.

284
00:18:20,491 --> 00:18:23,081
This army is done for already.

285
00:18:23,161 --> 00:18:26,791
Let's join Thorkell's army
and give him the prince as a gift.

286
00:18:26,871 --> 00:18:29,871
More than half of the other men are already on our side.

287
00:18:30,581 --> 00:18:33,041
We'll be able to convince the other half easily.

288
00:18:34,501 --> 00:18:35,961
You're going to betray him?

289
00:18:37,721 --> 00:18:39,381
Betray Askeladd?

290
00:18:39,931 --> 00:18:43,561
Don't call it a betrayal, Atli.

291
00:18:43,641 --> 00:18:46,391
He's a good leader. He's done a good job.

292
00:18:47,391 --> 00:18:50,561
That's why we're going to make him
take responsibility as the leader.

293
00:18:50,651 --> 00:18:53,731
We'll be fine! We'll be able to escape!

294
00:18:53,821 --> 00:18:55,981
We've always been able to escape, right?

295
00:18:56,071 --> 00:18:58,111
Well, up until now.

296
00:18:58,191 --> 00:19:00,361
But what about recently?

297
00:19:00,451 --> 00:19:03,201
He's made the wrong call, one after the other.

298
00:19:03,281 --> 00:19:05,031
He's run out of luck.

299
00:19:05,121 --> 00:19:07,911
And Thorkell found us,
even though we thought he was beat.

300
00:19:10,251 --> 00:19:12,081
Don't look at me like that.

301
00:19:13,081 --> 00:19:16,591
Well, you're right. He's a good leader.

302
00:19:17,461 --> 00:19:21,011
Then why did he mess with Thorkell?

303
00:19:21,091 --> 00:19:22,431
Brother...

304
00:19:22,511 --> 00:19:24,221
I'm not happy about this either.

305
00:19:25,221 --> 00:19:26,891
But we can't help it.

306
00:19:27,521 --> 00:19:29,891
Askeladd made a bet, and he lost.

307
00:19:30,811 --> 00:19:31,981
That's all.

308
00:19:43,201 --> 00:19:44,911
Good job.

309
00:19:45,531 --> 00:19:49,161
They're going to have a hard time getting their
sleds and cargo across.

310
00:19:49,251 --> 00:19:51,501
What if they abandon their cargo and keep chasing us?

311
00:19:51,581 --> 00:19:55,341
Then they're going to lose time finding food.

312
00:19:55,421 --> 00:19:57,961
They won't be able to follow us very far without eating.

313
00:19:58,961 --> 00:20:01,721
All right! Resume the march!

314
00:20:10,021 --> 00:20:10,851
They're here!

315
00:20:18,691 --> 00:20:20,401
Oh, I saw a flash!

316
00:20:41,091 --> 00:20:44,341
I...

317
00:20:44,431 --> 00:20:46,091
found you!

318
00:20:54,641 --> 00:20:56,651
-Unbelievable!
-No way...

319
00:20:56,731 --> 00:20:59,481
-A spear?
-Three of them? That's impossible!

320
00:20:59,571 --> 00:21:00,901
No! There were four of them!

321
00:21:00,981 --> 00:21:02,741
-This is bad.
-Damn! This is bad!

322
00:21:02,821 --> 00:21:04,321
-This is really bad!
-All right!

323
00:21:05,071 --> 00:21:07,701
Calm down, men!

324
00:21:07,781 --> 00:21:09,371
He's still far away.

325
00:21:09,451 --> 00:21:12,951
And we destroyed the bridge.
Forget about that spear just now.

326
00:21:13,041 --> 00:21:14,661
Bridge?

327
00:21:14,751 --> 00:21:16,501
What about the bridge?

328
00:21:16,581 --> 00:21:19,541
They'll be able to cross that river on foot!

329
00:21:19,631 --> 00:21:21,551
Destroying the bridge was useless!

330
00:21:21,631 --> 00:21:23,131
Is that what you think?

331
00:21:23,211 --> 00:21:25,721
If that's what you think,
then we're leaving right now.

332
00:21:25,801 --> 00:21:27,891
Every minute is precious.

333
00:21:29,641 --> 00:21:31,431
Not again!

334
00:21:31,511 --> 00:21:33,851
You keep saying march, march, march!

335
00:21:33,931 --> 00:21:35,941
Don't you know any other words?

336
00:21:36,021 --> 00:21:37,441
You!

337
00:21:40,021 --> 00:21:41,821
We can't win against Thorkell.

338
00:21:42,861 --> 00:21:45,111
Just bear with it for one more day.

339
00:21:45,191 --> 00:21:47,451
Destroying the bridge will start to pay off then.

340
00:21:49,241 --> 00:21:51,831
They can only march as fast as they can
carry their cargo.

341
00:21:51,911 --> 00:21:55,081
They're going to have trouble getting their cargo across.

342
00:21:55,161 --> 00:21:59,081
If they leave their cargo behind to chase us,
they won't be able to replenish supplies.

343
00:21:59,171 --> 00:22:02,171
They'll only be able to march for one day like that.

344
00:22:02,251 --> 00:22:03,841
Understand, men?

345
00:22:04,511 --> 00:22:06,471
If you understand, start marching!

346
00:22:06,761 --> 00:22:10,091
There's no guarantee we'll be able
to survive one more day!

347
00:22:16,431 --> 00:22:19,901
Oh, really? Then this is where we say goodbye.

348
00:22:19,981 --> 00:22:22,071
I'm in a hurry. Excuse me.
